  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). Independent check CORRECT. Behavioural proof: with DataModel.kind replaced by an object that raises on any access, `hypergumbo sketch` on a Django/Pydantic/dataclass fixture exited 0 and its output matched the plain run byte for byte (cache footer aside) -- deleting kind cannot change output. Corrections: (1) sketch reads symbol_id, framework, label, rank_score and confidence (_format_datamodels sketch.py:5811-5871, :6926-6945), not only symbol_id; none reads kind. (2) test_sketch.py has 9 DataModel(kind=...) constructors (:3151, 3169, 3186, 3202, 3218, 3239, 3241, 3243, 4965), not 2. (3) The 'cli-rust ValueEnum -> SCHEMA' mislabel cannot happen: _detect_from_concepts skips non-class symbols and Rust enums are kind='enum' (Qt model/view -> ORM_MODEL is plausible, qt.yaml:80). Sketch's double framework label is filed separately as WI-kibat. P4 kept."  # 169a
